From: macos-local research
Subject: [PATCH] Add a default-off guarded two-site ARM timeout diagnostic

An explicit private contract instruments two scalar FMOV-immediate sites.
A paused-only runtime base arms per-vCPU checks of actual PC, current address
space, UUID and bounded original code context. Reads reuse the ARM debug
walker with an ordinary-RAM-only path and reject unsupported regimes.
The replacement is fixed at 30.0 from 3.0. Guest bytes are not written.
Reset and post-load revoke arming; enabled profiles block migration.
No Apple addresses, UUIDs or instruction fingerprints are embedded here.
Local diagnostic experiment, not an original-deadline performance result
and not intended for upstream submission.

